    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0307" n="293" sameAs="frus:frus1950v06/pg293"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794A.5/1–2550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in China </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-01-25T17:00:00-05:00">January 25, 1950—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. Urtel 121 Jan 21.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d146-f1"/> Question flexibility being
                    explored with ECA. Dept believes, however, that significant progress in
                    direction Wu and Jen objectives possible only if Gimo aware such steps
                    indispensable survival Chi Govt Taiwan and takes determined forceful action
                    accordingly. Successive rewards within capacity US Govt cannot be decisive
                    factor and US Govt shld not place itself in position promising subsidize Chi
                    Govt through additional aid which attempted equate “sacrifices” Chi shld make in
                    own interests.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d146-f1" n="1" xml:id="d146-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed. In this telegram, Mr. Strong expressed support for the request of
                    ECA officials for flexibility in extending support, within the limits of
                    available U.S. funds, for the efforts of Governor Wu and Finance Commissioner
                    Jen toward resolving the Chinese Government’s financial deficit by reducing
                    military expenditures and the size of the military establishment. The particular
                    sentence in telegram 121 on which telegram 74 was commenting read as follows:
                    “Jen, although generally over-optimistic, truthfully believes he can get
                    Generalissimo make further reductions month by month if each time he can come up
                    with a little more from US as reward.” (894A.00R/1–2150)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
